;; 详情页/厂商页的正文内容词库。
;; 这里是"通用选购知识"部分 —— 从公开的 VPS 选购方法论提炼，属于行业通行做法，
;; 不冒充本站实测。真正独家的数字由 build.py 用本站 data/offers.json 现算。
;; 改文案只改这个文件，不要动 build.py。

::BLOCK{what_price_means|title:价格意味着什么 按价位档给一句解读}
  ;; 格式: 上限USD | 一句话。取第一个 >= 实际价格的档。
  3 | At this price point you are looking at the entry tier: shared vCPU, small RAM, and a monthly traffic allowance you should check before committing. It suits a single small site, a test box, or a lightweight service — not a busy production workload.
  8 | This sits in the mainstream band. Expect enough headroom for a personal site or a light app with caching in front of it, and a provider that treats renewal pricing as a normal part of the product rather than a first-year lure.
  20 | This is the mid tier. You are paying for either more resources, better network routing, or both. Worth it if real visitors depend on the box; overkill for a hobby project.
  45 | This is upper-mid. At this level the differentiator is almost always network quality and support, not raw CPU. Confirm what you are actually buying before paying for it.
  90 | This is a premium listing. At this price the plan usually bundles more cores and RAM than a small site needs, and the honest question is whether you are buying capacity or buying a bigger number.
  1000000 | This is a top-of-range listing. Listings this far above the entry tier are almost never about raw price-per-core — they are sized for real concurrent load, and they should be judged against what you actually need to serve.

::BLOCK{what_to_verify|title:下单前必须自己确认的三件事}
  ;; 全部是可执行动作，不是形容词
  Run a latency and packet-loss check against the provider's test IP from where your actual visitors are — not from where you are. A route that looks fine from your desk can collapse on a different carrier.
  Re-check the same measurement during the provider's evening peak. Averages taken at midday hide exactly the congestion you are trying to avoid.
  Read the renewal price, not just the first-term price, and add up two years of it. A headline number that only applies to the first billing cycle is not the number you will be paying.

::BLOCK{choosing_criteria|title:挑选时按这个顺序看 不要先看配置}
  Decide what the server is for before comparing specs. A box that only runs a scheduled job has completely different needs from one serving pages to visitors.
  Check the traffic allowance and what overage costs, before you check core count. Running out of monthly transfer is a harder failure than running out of CPU.
  Confirm whether the provider charges separately for a public IPv4 address, snapshots, or a data disk. These routinely change the real monthly cost.
  Verify the upgrade, downgrade, migration and refund rules in writing. Being able to upgrade does not imply you can downgrade later.
  Treat a snapshot as a rollback convenience, not a backup. If the instance is destroyed and the snapshot goes with it, you did not have a backup.

::BLOCK{common_traps|title:常见的几个坑}
  A low first-term price that reverts to a much higher renewal price is the single most common surprise. Record both numbers before you buy.
  Peak bandwidth and sustained throughput are different things. A large port number can coexist with a shared link, a monthly cap, or throttling after you exceed the allowance.
  Two plans with identical core and RAM counts can perform very differently depending on CPU scheduling, disk latency, and how loaded the neighbouring tenants are. A spec sheet does not settle this.
  Cheap annual prepay is how providers lock in customers, not a favour to you. On a provider you have not used before, start with the shortest term available.

::BLOCK{suitable_for|title:适合什么 不适合什么}
  Suitable: a personal website, an API endpoint, a webhook receiver, a scheduled automation job, or a light monitoring service.
  Not suitable: bulk media storage, a NAS replacement, continuous video transcoding, or GPU inference. A general-purpose VPS is the wrong resource type for those, and no amount of extra cores fixes it.

::BLOCK{how_we_got_this|title:这条数字怎么来的}
  The price above was read mechanically from the provider's own public page at the timestamp shown. It was extracted by matching the page's structured pricing data or a price pattern in the page text, and the exact source URL is listed above so you can check it yourself.
  Nothing on this page is estimated, averaged, or back-filled. Where the provider did not publish a machine-readable price, no price is shown rather than a guess.
  Ranking on this site is by published price only. No provider can pay to move up, and no listing is removed for commercial reasons.

::BLOCK{affiliate_note|title:联盟披露}
  Some outbound links on this site may be affiliate links. If you sign up through one, this site may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. Affiliate status does not affect which providers are listed, where they rank, or what price is displayed — the numbers are read from the providers' own pages either way.
